{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 15, :comments ["<b>To make atonement for your souls.</b> That you not be stricken through a census. Another interpretation — לְכַפֵּר עַל נַפְשׁוֹתֵיכֶם: because He hinted to them here three contributions — for תְּרוּמַת יְיָ is written here three times. One: the contribution of the sockets, which they counted when they began with the donation of the Mishkan — every single person gave a half-shekel, and it came to a hundred talents, as it says ״וְכֶסֶף פְּקוּדֵי הָעֵדָה מְאַת כִּכָּר״ (Exodus 38), and from them the sockets were made, as it says ״וַיְהִי מְאַת כִּכַּר הַכֶּסֶף״ וְגוֹ׳ (there). The second was also by census — they counted them once the Mishkan was erected; that is the census spoken of at the beginning of the book of Pekudim, ״בְּאֶחָד לַחֹדֶשׁ הַשֵּׁנִי בַּשָּׁנָה הַשֵּׁנִית״ (Numbers 1) — and every one gave a half-shekel, and they were to purchase from them the public offerings of every single year, and the poor and the rich were made equal in them. And concerning that contribution it says לְכַפֵּר עַל נַפְשׁוֹתֵיכֶם — for the offerings come for atonement. And the third is the contribution of the Mishkan, as it says ״כָּל מֵרִים תְּרוּמַת כֶּסֶף וּנְחֹשֶׁת״ (Exodus 35) — and all their hands were not equal in it, but each man whatever his heart volunteered."], :book :exodus, :voice :rashi, :lang :en, :chapter 30, :notes {}, :source-witnesses nil, :timestamp "2026-08-02T08:55:50.042280760Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}